1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,182
Borrow against Bitcoin on Mezo, and you do not get to choose when your
collateral gets redeemed.

2
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:10,130
The queue decides, worst collateral ratio first.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:13,968
This is the live book on Mezo right now.

4
00:00:13,917 --> 00:00:21,091
Three hundred sixty eight troves and four hundred twenty nine million
MUSD waiting behind the worst collateral ratios.

5
00:00:21,091 --> 00:00:23,722
The red ones are next in line.

6
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:27,365
The architect is where the move happens.

7
00:00:27,315 --> 00:00:30,740
Loop, unwind, exit, or shield.

8
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:33,852
One signature, one transaction.

9
00:00:36,429 --> 00:00:39,451
I am signed in as an outside user.

10
00:00:39,402 --> 00:00:49,805
This position opened this week, zero point zero four five Bitcoin of
collateral, two thousand two hundred forty one MUSD of debt, one fifty

11
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:53,246
A milli-Bitcoin more collateral.

12
00:00:53,197 --> 00:00:59,447
The x-ray prices it before anything is signed: post-loop position, the
fee, the slippage floor.

13
00:00:59,447 --> 00:01:02,338
Then one signature and one click.

14
00:01:02,338 --> 00:01:09,954
The flash borrows MUSD, the swap turns it into Bitcoin, the trove
takes on the new debt, and the pool is repaid from the swap.

15
00:01:09,954 --> 00:01:12,805
All of it inside one transaction.

16
00:01:12,805 --> 00:01:16,257
If any leg fails, the whole move reverts.

17
00:01:24,310 --> 00:01:30,301
Fifty two tests across the contracts, fuzzing on the reserve maths,
green on every push.

18
00:01:30,859 --> 00:01:34,599
Everything in this walkthrough is live on testnet today.

19
00:01:34,549 --> 00:01:40,916
The queue, the architect, five outside users with receipts, contracts
verified on Sourcify.

20
00:01:40,916 --> 00:01:43,207
Watch your place in line.

